From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dwrite: IDWriteTextLayout hit testing (HitTestTextRange, HitTestTextPosition, HitTestPoint)

The three hit testing methods of IDWriteTextLayout returned E_NOTIMPL, so text
editors and selection code built on DirectWrite (rich edit controls, XAML/WPF
text boxes, browsers, Direct2D applications) got no caret positions, no
selection rectangles and no click positions.

They work from the laid out clusters: the effective runs give the line, the
direction and the origin of each piece of text, the cluster metrics give the
widths, and the inline objects now remember the text positions they stand for.
 - HitTestTextRange returns one rectangle per piece of a line: the text of
   neighbouring runs of one line and one level is one rectangle (even with
   different font sizes), an inline object is a rectangle of its own that is not
   text, the range is cut at the end of the text, and a range that starts past the
   text is an empty rectangle at its end. Too small a buffer is
   E_NOT_SUFFICIENT_BUFFER with the needed count. The origin is added.
 - HitTestTextPosition gives the leading or trailing edge of the cluster at a text
   position (right to left clusters are the other way round) and the cluster's
   rectangle; a position past the end is the end of the last cluster.
 - HitTestPoint finds the line at the height of the point (the first or last one
   outside), then the cluster at its horizontal position, whether the point is in
   the second half of it (trailing) and whether it is inside the cluster.
White space at the end of a line hangs outside the runs; it is counted into the
last rectangle of the line for ranges.
---
--- a/dlls/dwrite/layout.c
